+| No usable report | No fabricated outcomes | 3. |
+
+Preserve existing exit precedence: no report → 3; otherwise policy violation → 1 even if analysis is also incomplete; otherwise incomplete/failed analysis or indeterminate policy → 2; otherwise 0. Without a policy, requested checks may still make analysis incomplete; severity/priority alone never selects exit 1. `verified_policy` requires affirmative provenance expectations; a policy permitting absence can yield policy pass while provenance remains absent. Unknown/unsupported expectations stay indeterminate. A registry publish attestation cannot satisfy a required build assertion; successful provenance cannot make source correspondence exact or clear unrelated conflicts. Offline reopening preserves the recorded verification time/root state rather than rechecking freshness.
