+### Independent evaluation design and thresholds
+
+**Scope of this retained design:** the original independent/held-out measurement design below is not a reviewer-recruitment gate after the current owner amendments. Development evaluation remains accepted within its authored-label/sample/leakage limits. Use these procedures only when producing an actual independent/held-out claim; no corresponding result is currently claimed.
+
+**Label authority and freeze for such a claim:** Shane owns acceptance and identifies an actual human reviewer independent of detector/rule authorship; use a second independent reviewer for consequential provenance/build explanations and disagreements. Reviewers see immutable source/artifact evidence and the rubric before outputs. Freeze labels, rationale, citation locations, allowed uncertainty, family membership, split seed/method and hashes before grading. Record each reviewer's actual role and adjudication; unresolved disagreements remain ambiguous labels. Agent-authored construction/golden labels help development but are never described as independent human review. Owner acceptance of Phase 1 labels is not independent Phase 2 evaluation.
+
+Approved minimum under P2-EVAL: 12 development families and 24 wholly separate held-out families, at least 120 held-out report observations, 30 per primary category and at least six families represented per category. Categories can have secondary tags; publish exclusive primary counts and overlapping subgroup counts separately. Group upstream project/monorepo, forks, related versions, common generated template/build recipe and every mutation derived from them into one family; no derivatives cross the split. If a shared template joins families, move the connected group as a whole. Keep existing public Phase 1 examples in development only. Human labeler/custodian retains held-out outputs; freeze code/config before one grading pass. A failure is retained; subsequent tuning needs a fresh family-separated reserve and newly declared gate, not repeated grading on the same test set.
+
+| Primary category | Cases and truth to establish independently | Denominator and intended measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| Benign/authored | Identical bytes, harmless formatting/metadata, legitimate script/entrypoint changes with documented significance | All eligible benign reports and all labeled field events; correct metadata observations are not false alarms merely because they are findings. |
+| Benign/generated | Lawfully retained minification/transpilation/bundling/layout differences and authored equivalent fixtures; include incomplete source/build context | All generated reports; separately the independently explainable subset and unsupported subset. Source/build evidence must support a relationship; generation labels do not authorize reproduced claims. |
+| Inert-mutated | Non-executing lifecycle add/change/remove, entrypoint edits, hidden extra bytes beside plausible generated output, wrong subject/source/policy fields | All seeded events by type and all mutated reports; mutation is construction truth, not a maliciousness label. Record exact retained old/new bytes and base-family links. |
+| Ambiguous/incomplete | Conflicting tags/manifest/override, absent source, unknown subtree/build recipe, omitted/corrupt members, parser limits, unsupported attestations and disputed labels | All ambiguous reports and each missing-scope reason; correct abstention and retention of uncertainty, not binary benign/malicious accuracy. |
+
+Lawful retention is a corpus entry gate: public availability alone is insufficient. Record origin URL/capture, full archive/member/source digests, immutable release/commit/subtree, permission/license/notice and allowed retention/redistribution scope. Keep original notices and immutable bytes; do not fetch/execute malware or retain private inputs. Select public licensed benign data and original inert mutations. If original bytes cannot lawfully be retained/reviewed, exclude the case before freeze and report the exclusion. This phase reads existing generated artifacts or constructs inert text; it does not execute a target build to create cases.
+
+Grade at separate units: report, supported field event, file/transform explanation, policy decision and factual claim/citation. Match an event by artifact/source identity + manifest pointer/change + rule class, once; duplicate parent/leaf findings cannot inflate true positives. Report TP/FP/FN and precision `TP/(TP+FP)` and recall `TP/(TP+FN)` for Q1/Q2 supported events and independently decidable explanation/policy classes. Missing outputs/abstentions on decidable events count as misses for unconditional recall. Report conditional precision/recall only alongside abstention and eligible coverage; zero denominators are N/A. Do not compute malware precision/recall from these categories or combine conformance mutation counts into a population accuracy claim.
+
+For each category and family report case/event/claim counts, exclusions, false escalations, unresolved outputs, unsupported scope, semantic omissions and full citation resolution/support counts. A false escalation is priority/significance above the independent rubric or an unsupported behavior/intent assertion; an honest raw difference is not automatically a false alarm. Measure direction, severity and priority agreement separately. Retain matrix of reason codes for abstention; AI-disabled is not model abstention. Report raw member/byte coverage and explanation coverage separately; unknown remaining archive scope has no invented denominator. A resolved citation must also entail the claimed value/direction/relationship; absence needs independently supported scope. Use family-weighted summaries and family-clustered uncertainty intervals alongside raw numerators/denominators; a tiny zero-error sample is not proof of zero risk.
+
+These are the **originally approved P2-EVAL targets**, not measured results. Current owner amendments remove reviewer recruitment/signoff as blocking gates. Actual independent labels and a freeze remain necessary before calling a result independent/held-out:
+
+| Metric / class | Proposed threshold and minimum evidence |
+|---|---|
+| Critical truth/compatibility boundary | Zero cryptographically verified provenance for wrong artifact/subject; zero `verified_policy` or policy pass for unmet required expectations. Valid cryptographic-only results may coexist with policy rejection. Zero concealed conflicts/omissions, invented execution/reproduction/safety claims, changed historical bytes or cross-interface outcome upgrades. Every mandatory negative fixture must pass. |
+| Q1/Q2 event quality | Per rule class precision and unconditional recall ≥95%; direction accuracy 100% for resolved supported events; severity and priority agreement each ≥95%. At least 10 independently labeled additions, 10 changes and 10 removals per rule class in held-out data; unresolved cases counted separately. |
+| Q3 explanations and false escalation | Supported explanation precision ≥95%; explain at least 70% of independently explainable generated cases. False escalation ≤5% separately in benign and benign-generated categories (with 30 reports, at most one in each). Unexplained residuals stay visible regardless of score. |
+| Uncertainty and resolvability | Preserve unresolved status in 100% of mandatory ambiguous/missing-scope cases; resolve ≥95% of supported, intact in-budget Q1/Q2 events. Record abstention for every category and stage; no aggregate abstention cap that pressures unsafe guesses. |
+| Citation support | 100% of graded factual observations/explanations have valid cited evidence and independently supported claims; zero out-of-member ranges or invented absence. Missing content yields qualified metadata, never fabricated bytes. |
+| Provenance/policy conformance | 100% expected outcomes for every supported positive/negative fixture and actual exit path; at least two real npm positives per admitted provider/format. Publish count per failure mode; do not label this held-out population accuracy. |
+
+If category/event/family minima are unavailable, the corresponding statistical acceptance is unestablished; no pass on a smaller denominator is invented. Reviewer staffing/signoff is waived for amended local acceptance, while independent/held-out claims still require actual evidence. Owner may amend gates prospectively with reasons before grading; never lower a threshold after inspecting held-out scores. Broader package popularity/generalization and resource/SLO claims remain unestablished by this bounded corpus.
